# What Prettier must never rewrite in this repository.
#
# Prettier's job here is narrow: the hand-written TypeScript under
# crates/candid-core-ts/ts/. Everything below is either generated, compared
# byte for byte by a test, or not ours — and every entry is a file Prettier
# *would* have changed, not a precaution against a hypothetical.
#
# Prettier also honours .gitignore by default, so /target/, node_modules/, and
# /candid-scope/ are already out. They are repeated here so that an invocation
# passing --ignore-path (which replaces the default list rather than adding to
# it) still fails closed.

# Generator output, compared byte for byte by `cargo test -p candid-core-ts
# --features compiler`. Prettier reformats 6 of the 10 goldens (152 lines), so
# formatting them turns the golden suite red and, worse, would silently move
# the reviewed mapping decisions these files record. The emitter owns their
# layout; regenerate with UPDATE_GOLDENS=1, never with a formatter.
/crates/candid-core-ts/tests/goldens/

# Conformance and artifact-identity vectors are digests of exact octets
# (docs/artifact-identity-v1.md). .gitattributes already pins their line
# endings across platforms for this reason; reformatting the JSON would move
# every pinned artifact ID.
/tests/fixtures/

# Reviewed measurement records, not source: reformatting them would make a
# baseline diff unreadable at exactly the moment it matters (docs/benchmarks.md).
/benches/baselines/

# Build output of `npm run build`, and the packaged-consumer fixture's tree.
/crates/candid-core-ts/ts/dist/

# Documentation page fragments. Inside a <pre> the text is taken literally by
# website/build.mjs and escaped on the way out, so a sample containing
# `Vec<TypeNode>` or `Option<&str>` is correct source that Prettier's HTML
# parser cannot read: it reports `Unexpected closing tag "pre"` and refuses the
# file. The generated pages under website/dist/ do parse, and are already
# covered by the /website/dist/ entry in .gitignore. Everything else in
# website/ — the CSS, the generator, the checker, the site script — is
# formatted by this same Prettier and must stay that way.
/website/content/

# Restated from .gitignore so --ignore-path invocations stay safe.
node_modules/
/target/
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/candid-scope/
